// Rule: Windows - Repeated Failed Logons (Brute Force)
// MITRE: T1110 Brute Force / T1110.001 Password Guessing (Credential Access)
// Schedule: every 5 min, lookback 10 min | Severity: Medium
// Entities: IP = IpAddress, Host = Computer
// Incident settings: alert grouping on (match all entities, 5 h), suppression OFF
//
// Tuning history:
//  - Original version (no LastIngested filter) created 2 alerts / 2 incidents per burst
//    (10 min lookback / 5 min frequency = 2 runs saw the same burst).
//  - Day 16: added the LastIngested filter below. 2 tests (8 failed logons each) produced
//    1 alert and 1 incident each. Alerts arrived about 7-10 min after ingestion.
//  - Not safe to use a plain ingestion_time() filter on the events (as the sudo rule does):
//    the count must still use the whole lookback window, so only the trigger is gated.
SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4625
| summarize Failures = count(), Users = make_set(TargetUserName), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated), LastIngested = max(ingestion_time()) by IpAddress, Computer
| where Failures >= 5
| where LastIngested > ago(5m)
